<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ADR-039 amendment — deterministic (fact) vs advisory (probabilistic) grounding tiers</title>
    <phase>0 Governance Gate</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>ADR amendment (architecture/governance change); merge gate blocking all advisory-tier tasks; high blast radius across dispatch.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>ADR-migration / governance authoring with cross-cutting downstream impact (Step 3.5.5b opus trigger: architectural change + ADR-amendment work).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches .claude/adr/ and docs/adr/ and .claude/CHANGELOG.md — main-session-only (sub-agent write boundary). Also a sequential merge gate.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>adr, governance, ai, documentation</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Amend ADR-039 to formally differentiate a deterministic (fact-based, verbatim-cited) grounding tier from
    an advisory (probabilistic, full-reasoning) grounding tier. This is CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path B and is the merge
    gate (FR-00): no advisory-tier code in this project merges before this amendment lands. The advisory tier
    must still be prompt-controlled, citation-required, and carry a "not legal advice" posture.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform architect. Expert in the ADR-039 grounded-execution model, closed Actions/Bindings/Tools
    catalogs, and the CLAUDE.md §6.5 ADR conflict-resolution protocol. Author concise + full ADR versions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Both ADR-039 versions (concise `.claude/adr/` + full `docs/adr/`) describe two grounding tiers with explicit
    MUST/MUST NOT rules; `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` records the amendment; adr-check passes; downstream advisory-tier
    tasks can cite this amendment as their governance basis.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The north star is Claude/ChatGPT-level advisory output that deliberately relaxes Spaarke's default
      deterministic guardrails for interactive, human-verified analysis/advisory paths — while remaining accurate
      and cited. ADR-039 today mandates strict grounded/closed-catalog determinism, which would flag the advisory
      NDA-review path as a violation. This amendment creates a sanctioned lane for it. See spec.md FR-00 and the
      ADR Tensions section (ADR-039 → Path B).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file>projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1/spec.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>None — this is the first task and the merge gate.</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-6.5">This amendment is Path B. Both the concise and full ADR versions must be updated together; the amendment merges before or alongside any dependent advisory-tier code in this project.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">The advisory tier MUST remain prompt-controlled, MUST require a citation for every factual claim, and MUST decline unverifiable claims. It relaxes verbatim-grounding determinism, NOT accuracy or auditability. The ADR-040 session ledger (store-before-render) still applies to advisory output.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT weaken auth, security, or the closed Actions/Bindings/Tools catalog model — the amendment is about output determinism, not catalog governance.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/adr-check/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="ADR amendment (concise+full)" location=".claude/skills/ai-procedure-maintenance/SKILL.md">
        Author the concise `.claude/adr/` constraint version and the full `docs/adr/` rationale version together; keep MUST/MUST NOT rules identical in intent.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Read both ADR-039 versions and the spec.md ADR Tensions section to capture the exact MUST/MUST NOT rules the advisory path challenges.</step>
    <step order="2">Draft the amendment: a named "Advisory (probabilistic) tier" alongside the existing "Deterministic (fact) tier", with a decision rule for which tier an Action runs under, and the advisory tier's non-negotiables (citation-required, decline-if-unverifiable, not-legal-advice, ledger-still-applies).</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the amendment to the full `docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md` (rationale + examples) and the concise `.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md` (MUST/MUST NOT only).</step>
    <step order="4">Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` if the ADR summary line changed; add a dated entry to `.claude/CHANGELOG.md`.</step>
    <step order="5">Run adr-check against the amended ADR to confirm internal consistency.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 001 ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If differentiating the tiers requires changing the closed-catalog or auth model (not just output determinism), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6/§6.5 — that is beyond this amendment's scope.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run adr-check and git.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</output>
    <output type="docs">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Both ADR-039 versions define a deterministic tier and an advisory tier with explicit MUST/MUST NOT rules and a decision rule for tier selection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The advisory tier's rules require a citation per factual claim, decline-if-unverifiable, and a not-legal-advice posture; the ADR-040 ledger obligation is preserved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has a dated entry describing the amendment as CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path B.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">adr-check reports no internal inconsistency in the amended ADR-039.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No change to the closed-catalog, auth, or security model is introduced (verified by diff review).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This is a merge gate: FR-00. Downstream tasks 020/023/031/040/041 rely on it as the governance basis for
    relaxed-determinism advisory output. Sub-agents cannot write `.claude/` — this task is main-session-only.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all knowledge files before starting. Follow task-execute pre-execution checklist. Human review required before merge (governance change per CLAUDE.md §6).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
